        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: رعایا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رعایا — riāyā — \"the subjects (of a ruler)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رعایا بادشاہ سے ناراض تھی۔ riāyā bādshāh se nārāz thī. The king's subjects were angry with him."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رعایا (riāyā) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic raʿāyā, the plural of raʿiyya, \"a flock, the people in one's care\". Urdu treats it as one feminine body: رعایا ناراض تھی."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
